ing that i had and i  had four cardboard boxes  that i shipped out to hawaii i did not  know a single person i was actually  supposed to move out there with  a good friend and then at the last  minute her parents were like  we'll get you an apartment and a car if  you'll stay so she stayed  sad very sad but it all worked out  anyway i ended up going to school in  hawaii the university of hawaii manoa  and i studied uh business so i got my  bachelor of business administration and  i also got  a minor in spanish and  oh my gosh probably the best decision  i've ever made in my whole life  was going to school in hawaii  it was very expensive i remember  specifically a gallon of milk was seven  dollars i ended up  working a ton of different jobs first i  started working at  abercrombie fitch as a model while going  to school full-time  and then i also picked up a job as a  waitress i ended up working at  i think like four or five different  restaurants then i also started modeling  and that paid the bulk of my bills um i  did like  magazines runway uh i was an extra  lost i hosted events for like rolex  and um oh i did one for tiffany's oh no  sorry harry winston  that was really fun they like put me in  this big gown and i had to wear  diamonds and walk around and people  would buy them and  weird stuff yeah and also craigslist  gigs i got you know like some hosting  jobs  i worked as a retail manager at puma and  also starbucks and ended up back at  abercrombie which i loved i ended up  working with them for eight years  in hawaii managing two different stores  and then i went to california  colorado ohio and kentucky and then  i asked my manager if there was any way  i could move up to the international  team so i interviewed for that  and that's when things really changed i  went over to  london and i managed um the flagship  store there and then i was sent to italy  meanwhile i was taking italian lessons  so i also speak fluent italian when i  showed up  at the store in italy i just it was a  completely different dialect than what i  had learned company italian is very like  um  it's very different being fully immersed  in a different country  not only having to like function as an  adult and  a member of society there like learning  how to say how do i turn on my heat  to communicate job duties and build  relationships  i had a great time there i learned a lot  one of those things being that the  corporate life was not for me when that  contract ended  i just took time off i shipped all my  stuff from my southern  italian apartment to a storage unit in  the us and  i just took a backpack and started  traveling and that turned into 11 months  of traveling i ended up going around the  world like that wasn't intentional  just kept going from country to country  started dating someone in the middle  east  and we moved together to monterey  california  um i again didn't know anyone there but  he had a job offer there so  he was like do you want to move in  together so i started looking around at  different retail positions  and i just realized that my heart wasn't  in it like i'd do anything to  not have to go back to that nine to five  lifestyle  so what i ended up doing is what i had  done in college i just went on  craigslist and started looking at gig  listings  and there was this local artist slash  painter  photographer that was looking for an  assistant to work just six hours a week  i did everything from like  clearing out her garage to applying for  her  dual citizenship in a different country  to  sending out email newsletters helping  with social media  uh contacting pr people she generously  introduced me to her friends  and over time i built a clientele list  of 12  different like artists videographers  painters sculptors  small business owners and that was  amazing i was loving it but at the same  time i was really falling in love with  big sur and taking photos and exploring  the area and i was  really really wantin